GRAMMAR.md §4.2, §5.9 pastType, TYPES.md §8.4, DECISIONS 304 (log-2026-10-05 "304 implementation rulings"): `past` followed on its line by a token that can start a type, other than `(`, `{`, `from` and `keyed`, is a pastType, held as the Past token of the primary type after it: a name (`past X(args)` keeps its typeArgs, `past V?` is `(past V)?`), `ref`, a list (its typeArgs and `keyed by` outside), a table, a stable table, a function type, an asset, a type-level match, a string literal and `_`, so that check can judge them (E3024). Anywhere else `past` is an identifier: a type named `past` (alone, qualified `past.K`, before `?`, `|`, `)`, `,`, `{` of a fn body, `from env`, `keyed by` or a line break), a type function named `past` (`past(1..)`), the name after `past past`, a field, a let, a parameter and an expression named `past`. `past {K: V}` is the type `past` and a stray brace, `past keyed by id` a keyed name (E1137) and `[past` before a line break a name (d.canon). A second `past` is a name, so `past past X` leaves X stray (e.canon).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

record Role {
    kinds: [past GrantKind]
    sold: [past ref items]
    last: past V?
    oldest: past GrantKind where it != GrantKind.a
    pair: {past GrantKind: past ref items}
    either: past A | B
    refined: past a.Code(1..)
    past: past
    plain: past?
    named: past.Kind
    twice: past past
    paren: (past GrantKind)
    fun: fn(past GrantKind) -> past ref items
    alone: past
    next: Int
    secret: input past from env "X"
}

type Old = past GrantKind
type Alias = past | past.Kind
type Fn = past(1..)
let past: past = past + 1
fn f(past: past, k: past) -> (past) { return past }
fn g() -> past { return 1 }
-- b/b.canon --
package b

type L = past [Int]
type K = past [Event](..=3) keyed by id
type T = past table T
type S = past stable table T
type F = past fn(Int) -> Int
type A = past asset("@resource/Icon")
type X = past match n { a => Int, _ => String }
type Q = past "lit" | "other"
type U = past _
-- d/d.canon --
package d

type M = past {String: Int}
type B = past keyed by id
type N = [past
    GrantKind]
-- e/e.canon --
package e

type P = past past X
-- ast --
